&lt;p style="margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Based on long-term firm contracts in place on September 1, 2022, the settlement result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;incremental &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;reductions in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;revenues of $2.8 million in 2024 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;$1.8 million in 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Brookfield, Connecticut Site Clean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Up&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 2pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On June 27, 2003, the Partnership purchased real property in Brookfield, Connecticut upon which it constructed its Brookfield compressor station (Brookfield Site or Site). On November 3, 2004, the Connecticut Department of Energy and Environmental Protection (DEEP) approved the Site&amp;#8217;s remediation plan and scope of work schedule. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;After the m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ajor clean-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;up, re-grading, and seeding work at the Brookfield Site was &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; (with the exception of buried tires on the property which is discussed below), Iroquois received a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Letter of No Audit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; (LNA)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; from the DEEP dated November 13&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, 2014&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; The LNA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; states that the DEEP agrees with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Iroquois&amp;#8217;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Licensed Environmental Professional (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;LEP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; that the site is now clean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; (with the exception of the buried tires on the property) and closes the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Environmental Condition Assessment Form (ECAF) for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Brookfield Voluntary Cleanup.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For the remaining buried tires on the Brookfield site&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, Iroquois has entered into the state Stewardship Prog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ram.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Stewardship Program &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;requires monitoring of the tire area &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;until 2041 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and remediation of any erosion, subsidence, or tires that have worked their way to the surface&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; It is not anticipated that the ongoing monitoring of this site will have a material effect on the Partnership&amp;#8217;s financial condition or results of operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 2pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Enhancement by Compression Project (ExC)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During 2019 the Partnership entered into precedent agreements with Con Edison and KeySpan Gas East Corporation d/b/a National Grid to develop and permit incremental pipeline delivery capacity to transport additional volumes of natural gas along Iroquois&amp;#8217; system to support design day demand and the reliability needs of their systems. The project optimizes the Iroquois system to meet current and future gas supply needs of utility customers while minimizing environmental impact through compressor enhancements at existing compressor stations along the pipeline thereby avoiding land disturbances outside of existing facility footprints. The project&amp;#8217;s total capacity is approximately 125,000 Dth/day and it is 100% underpinned by 20-year term contracts. This project require&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; FERC and various federal and state permits. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) issued an order of public convenience and necessity for ExC on March 25, 2022. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On October 28, 2024, Iroquois requested FERC to issue an Order granting an extension of time until March 25, 2027, to complete the construction of the ExC Project and place the facilities into service. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The FERC granted Iroquois&amp;#8217; request by Order dated February 19, 2025. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On February 7, 2025, the Partnership received th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; necessary state air permits from the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation for each of the Athens and Dover Compressor Stations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;In Connecticut, on July 29, 2025, the Department of Energy &amp;amp; Environmental Protection (CT DEEP) issued a Notice of Tenative Determination to approve the Iroquois air permits. There were three petitions (Petitioners) requesting an adjudicatory hearing. All three requests were denied by the CT DEEP Hearing Officer (the Ruling). The Petitioners appealed the Ruling and filed a Motion to Stay with the Connecticut Superior Court, Judicial District of New Britain. Both matters were heard by the Court on February 17, 2026. On March 12, 2026 the Connecticut Superior Court dismissed the appeals. The public informational hearing was held on January 8, 2026, with an additional comment period ending on January 15, 2026. The public comments are under review by the CT DEEP. The CT DEEP will file a response to the public comments on or before April 13, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; project is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; projected &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;to be placed in service in calendar year 2028&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. The estimated project cost including AFUDC is $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;380&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; million and upon receipt of all outstanding permits shall be revised in accordance with the terms and conditions set forth in precedent agreements executed with the project shippers. As of December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, the Partnership has incurred approximately $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; million of engineering and permitting related capital expenditures, including AFUDC. The Company currently believes it will obtain all necessary approvals for the project. However, in the event such permits are not granted, the Partnership expects to recover 50% of the expenditures incurred to date based upon agreements with third parties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Property Tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Nassau County Property Tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt; Settlement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In January 2023, 2024, and 2025, Iroquois received and paid under protest tax bills representing the State of New York, Nassau County Tax Collection imposing real property taxes or special ad valorem levies upon Iroquois Property for the Nassau County Sewer Collection and Disposal District.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Iroquois pipeline is not located within the boundaries of the Nassau County Sewer District.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Iroquois filed complaints in April 2023, and 2024 challenging the sewer collection and disposal charges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;By Settlement Agreement dated March 20, 2025, The State of New York, Nassau County agreed to reimburse Iroquois approximately $0.6 million as full settlement of all improperly imposed taxes assessed and billed on Iroquois Property as part of the Nassau County Sewer and Disposal District&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;for the tax years 2023, 2024 and 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The State of New York Nassau County also agreed not to include the Iroquois Property in the District commencing with the 2026 county/town tax bills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Iroquois received payment in full from the State of New York in June 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; has recorded the benefit as a reduction of Taxes Other Than Income on the consolidated Statements of Comprehensive Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 1pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Bronx Property Tax Assessment Settlement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On March 1, 2024, the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; filed an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;administrative &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;appeal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and a judicial petition on October 16, 2024,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of the tax assessment of a portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; its Bronx facilities (known as the Eastchester Extension) with the Tax Commission of the City of New York (NYC Tax Commission)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; for the tax period ending June 30, 2025. On October 15, 2025, a petition was filed appealing the tax assessment for the tax period ending June 30, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The two matters were consolidated, and a hearing was held on both matters on September 30, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; (Consolidated Tax Appeals)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On February 12, 2026 the NYC Tax Commission proposed, and Iroquois accepted an assess&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ed property value &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;of $3,000,000 for both years resulting in a settlement of the Consolidated Tax Appeals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The table below is representative of the results of the settlement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;
&lt;table style="margin-right: auto; margin-left: auto; border: 0.75pt solid #000000; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
