  <ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock id="HH8533368EB711634BB3DF2FE4E4CB89D5" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfApplicableNotesTextBlock>
  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="HHD83F070B97EA6422D24ABE6610ADFB02" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;Construction Overheads: Employee benefits (burdened costs) are allocated to construction projects based on actual payroll charged to each specific project. There is no allocation made for indirect labor and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;Allowance of Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC): The allowance of funds used during construction consists, in general, of the cost of borrowed funds used for construction purposes and a reasonable rate of return on other funds when used. The allowance is determined by applying the capitalization rate to construction work orders. Capitalization begins at the time the company begins continuous accumulation of costs in construction work orders on a planned, progressive basis and ends when the facilities are placed in service for which constructed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
