    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HHF501AFF49737EEC20ED86C6A7AA829B1" xlink:to="HH0B66FB3977C532921A3CBDC2F9BADB65" order="1" />
    <link:loc xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="#HH5E980429840C55CE7F75E9D6A5995C05" xlink:label="HH5E980429840C55CE7F75E9D6A5995C05" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HH065E8DFDB9F2B9675A738F6560F85A74" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Page 332, Line 16, column (c) note


Iroquois charges fuel-in-kind based on Monthly Fuel &amp; Losses Retention (F&amp;LR) Factors.  Over/under collections of natural gas are trued-up through adjustments to the F&amp;LR Factors that Iroquois charges its customers in future months pursuant to Section 36 of the General Terms and Conditions of Iroquois&#8217; FERC Gas Tariff.

As a result, no cash is transferred between Iroquois and Iroquois&#8217; shippers for fuel and measurement variances including Lost and Unaccounted for Gas.

Iroquois delivers gas to TGP and AGT for fuel as fuel-in-kind.

Iroquois has valued the gas reported as indicated on Page 521 et al. (in this Form 2 and in previous Form 3-Q filings for 2025) for each month in the year using the PAL and HUB Credit Index Price in effect for each month.  

</div>
    </link:footnote>
